  "conclusions": [
    "Known all-NTT1 seed 7302 reproduces 16/16 NTT1 jobs but has only a 1.02166x single-pair gain; first and return M32 paired medians regress.",
    "M128 loses five of six timing pairs; M256 loses all six. The unchanged M16 control has a near-neutral 1.00212x paired median.",
    "Separate single profiles support the rejection direction at M128/M256 (183.359 to 193.831 us; 224.050 to 238.184 us), but are not causal measurements.",
    "Same REG96 and zero STACK/LOCAL for both main kernels provide no evidence for a spill-based explanation. The failed performance hypothesis is sufficient to stop."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One prepared weight seed and six fresh input pairs per case; no official confidence interval.",
    "Single profiles use a separate fresh input and do not enter timing medians.",
    "Standalone MoE routing is not decoder routing; the decoder counterpart has not been run.",
    "Read-sweep selfcheck verifies observable loads, not measured cold DRAM traffic.",
    "Ratios of separate latency medians can differ from the median of paired ratios; decisions use paired ratios."
  ],
